_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.04471249795158817,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":18.4,"_gate_pool_share":-0.3637033648169232,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.13782426965705785,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.03929792583663553,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":10.7,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.24478882224890905,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.12831042743207033,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012703365277468242,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.0102699995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Centrus Energy Corp. supplies nuclear fuel components for the nuclear power industry in the United States, Japan, the Netherlands, and internationally. The company operates through two segments: Low-Enriched Uranium (LEU) and Technical Solutions. The LEU segment sells separative work units (SWU) components of LEU; natural uranium hexafluoride, uranium concentrates, and uranium conversion; and enriched uranium products to utilities that operate nuclear power plants. The Technical Solutions segment offers technical, manufacturing, engineering, and operations services to public and private sector customers. It also operates as a equipment manufacturing and engineering firm focused primarily on the energy sector. Additionally, it manufactures and ships centrifuges to Oak Ridge to support a major expansion of its uranium enrichment capacity in Ohio. The company was formerly known as USEC Inc. and changed its name to Centrus Energy Corp. in September 2014. Centrus Energy Corp. was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Bethesda, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Amir V. Vexler | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 467 people. Revenue per employee of $961K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, declining at 10%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $67K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Centrus Energy Corp. is a mid-cap energy business with a $2.1B market cap on $449M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $31M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.66\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 24.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 58% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.582316325097954},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (30.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 4091% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Centrus Energy surges as Roth raises to Buy as near-term concerns subside (LEU:NYSE)","source":"seekingalph